Save93 / AE 1.6.1170 / SSE Display Tweaks 0.5.16 limiter 30 FPS / Papyrus bEnableLogging=1 / APB_GAMEPLAY_TRACE=catchup-soak, APB_CATCHUP_MODE=accelerate, target 60, EngageBelowFPS 50 / APB_SOAK_JB1=1
Chatty NPCs.esp: JB1ClearAlias (on the reference aliases of JB1FollowerGreeting 0x8C2, JB1ChattyFollowers 0x8B8 and others) is
    event OnCellDetach()  GetOwningQuest().Stop()  Clear()  endEvent
  Stop() only requests the stop; Clear() on a non-optional alias of a quest that is still running logs 'Cannot clear a non-optional alias'.
  These quests are started by topic-info fragments (ChatGo.Start()) when NPCs speak, so in normal play whether one runs at a cell change is chance.
Probe: 4 s before each trip the harness starts JB1FollowerGreeting and JB1ChattyFollowers. jb1-* runs used the console 'startquest';
  jb1b-* runs call TESQuest::Start (the engine call behind startquest) and log its result, the state 0.5 s later, before travel, 11 s after arrival and at the end.
  A quest is running when stopped:false (TESQuest::IsStopped); alias values are the filled references (00000000 = empty).
Every attempt is listed. jb1-acc-2 stalled before the save loaded: skse64.log ends after kDataLoaded was sent to SexLabUtil.dll (handle 257); the next plugin never received it.
  VM catch-up cannot run at that point (no save loaded, gate closed); no hang dump exists, so the stall's cause is unconfirmed.
Test DLLs: jb1-* c1a0db3d9352940f8de3044b7edb13968db757e078200eaf1fd98482b7f3c7a0, jb1b-* ec0791d486c58efff5d10be5941a078a1eb870548024e1aca309887564b4d708 (same VMCatchUp source as release 25429bd8...).
